# Chaos: loot beams (client/BASE.md 0069; after 0001-0068). A thin light pillar over a tile and a soft glow pool at its base, drawn by MapView with additive blending (ONE, ONE) and two textures made at start from the profiles in the new header src/client/lootbeam.h (no sprites, no new pair). The pool goes on the camera floor after the tile's bottom layer (over the corpse, under the creatures) with a small light of its colour; the pillar goes in drawMapForeground after the light view (a dark cave does not swallow it) and before the names, bars and texts, clipped to the map, skipped under a drawn roof. Both pulse gently by the clock and follow walking and zoom like the map. Lua: g_map.setLootBeam(pos, color, heightTiles, intensity) (false at the cap of 64), g_map.removeLootBeam(pos), g_map.clearLootBeams(), g_map.getLootBeamCount(), g_map.hasLootBeam(pos); Map::clean clears them. The overlay module game_lootbeams sets them. C++ only.
